= The Prisons of the Republic

In the aftermath of the October rising, some thirty thousand prisoners fill the jails of a Republic that only three years ago promised liberty. The Asturian coalfields are placed under a state of war; the Army of Africa's Moorish regiments and the Legion, brought to the mainland by a rising general named Franco, conduct a repression the country will not forget. Torture in the Oviedo barracks becomes a national scandal.

The <span style="color: #c00000;">**PSOE**</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">**UGT**</span> leadership - Largo Caballero among them - are imprisoned or in hiding. Yet from the cells a strange strength grows: October gives the left its martyrs, its prison-poetry, and a slogan for the elections to come - *amnistía*. The Popular Front is being forged in these jails.

[? if left_dissent >= 40 : Our own base no longer wants coalition and compromise; it wants the prisoners freed and the guilty punished. ?]
